# Perez-Gonzalez et al. (2025), "The Rise of the Galactic Empire: Ultraviolet Luminosity Functions at z~17 and
#   z~25 Estimated with the MIDIS+NGDEEP Ultra-deep JWST/NIRCam Dataset", ApJ 991, 179 (2025),
#   doi:10.3847/1538-4357/adf8c9
# arXiv:2503.15594v4 (published version), Table 3 (tab:lf, "Luminosity function data points")
# Survey: MIDIS NIRCam parallel + NGDEEP (5-sigma depth ~31.5 mag); F200W / F277W dropouts; Vmax method
# x: M_UV = absolute magnitude averaged in a 0.01 um window around 0.15 um (= M1500), no dust correction;
#    0.75 mag bins
# Phi: log10(phi / Mpc^-3 mag^-1); asymmetric 1-sigma errors in dex (Monte Carlo M_UV/photo-z + cosmic
#      variance in quadrature)
# Cosmology: H0 = 70, Om = 0.3, OL = 0.7
# Redshift: z~25 (F277W dropouts, roughly 24 < z < 28); bins typically contain ~2 objects
# Excluded: brightest bin M=-18.99 is an upper limit (log phi < -4.6) -> Perez-Gonzalez2025_ulimit/
# Effective volumes [1e4 Mpc^3]: 4.7, 1.8
# M_UV   log10(phi)   sigma_upper(dex)   sigma_lower(dex)
-18.24  -4.82  0.31  0.75
-17.49  -4.66  0.33  1.11
